\newlabel{fig:features}{{3}{5}{Top-firing residues for four leading hazard-aligned SAE features in RFD3 block 12, rendered on partial-diffusion output structures. Color indicates feature activation: red = highest, orange = moderate, gray = inactive (PyMOL cartoon view). Feature 639 shows the three highest-activation residues (99, 104, 109) clustered within a single alpha-helix of ammodytoxin A, a presynaptic viper neurotoxin. Feature 60 fires sparsely on a Monkeypox virus immunoevasion phosphatase. Features 170 and 351 show scattered activation on a plant toxin and a mosquito salivary toxin, respectively.\relax }{figure.caption.4}{}}
\newlabel{fig:features@cref}{{[figure][3][]3}{[1][4][]5}}
